## Independent authentication of current evidence

The independent standard-library checker check_completed.py does not invoke or import a compiler. It directly rehashes the original and frozen sources, stdout/stderr, original and cache receipts, exact source/import companion bundles, compiler identity, present native libraries, cache-key inputs, and the gzip artifacts. It confirms that every record corresponds to the intended graph's literal import set and to a completed FRESH_KERNEL_PASS event.

Every compressed entry was streamed through full decompression, checking both its uncompressed SHA-256 and byte length against the unchanged original receipt. All 70 records passed:

- 840,584,950 original trace bytes;
- 17,099,862 compressed bytes;
- 884 distinct current file hashes checked.

Independent result:
